    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110-a1">

                <pb facs="0243" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg153"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    304.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rivas to Mr. Williamson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Office of Minister of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1875-01-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 8, 1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For your information, I do myself the honor
                    to inclose to your excellency two printed copies of the correspondence had with
                    the Costa Rican cabinet in reference to the acts done in Nicaraguan territory by
                    the forces of that republic.</p>
                <p>My government is pleased to believe that your excellency will appreciate in their
                    true worth the motives that have guided it in bringing forward its reclamation
                    for acts that it has believed to be offensive to the sovereign dignity of the
                    nation, as well as to the fraternal sentiments that should animate the republic
                    of Costa Rica, and to its sincere desire of putting an end to the annoying and
                    prejudicial questions that separate it with this government.</p>
                <p>In the hope that your excellency will co-operate for the consummation of this end
                    that is interesting to the peace of Central America, I have the honor of
                    offering to your excellency the distinguished consideration with which I
                    subscribe myself,</p>
                <p>Your excellency’s attentive servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. H. RIVAS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. Williamson</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister of the United States in Central
                            America.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
